## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design runtime pluggability, concurrency, and evolution of a caching layer.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern for eviction
- Registry-based runtime switching
- Thread-safety and atomic swaps
- Migration path for existing data

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Cache<K,V> {
  get(key: K): V | undefined
  set(key: K, value: V): void
  swapStrategy(name: string): void
}

interface EvictionStrategy<K,V> {
  onAccess(key: K, value: V): void
  onInsert(key: K, value: V): void
  evict(container: Map<K,V>): void
}

class Registry<K,V> {
  private map = new Map<string, EvictionStrategy<K,V>>();
  register(name: string, s: EvictionStrategy<K,V>) { this.map.set(name, s) }
  get(name: string): EvictionStrategy<K,V> | undefined { return this.map.get(name) }
}
```

